<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112557" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φύ̄λαρχ-ος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>chief officer of a</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῡλή,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.2.14
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>BMus.Inscr.</u>
				1005
			</span></i> (Cyzic.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				3773
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Nicomedia</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sammelb.</u>
				6257
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(v/vi A. D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			= Lat. <i>tribunus militum,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				2.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Rom.</u>
				20
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>c.</b>
			<i>chief priest</i> of a tribe among the Jews, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>1 Es.</u>
				7.8
			</span></i>: pl., <i>elders</i> of a tribe, ib.<i><span class="en">
				<u>De.</u>
				31.28
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>d.</b>
			<i>sheikh,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν Ἀράβων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					16.1.28
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Procop.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				1.19
			</span></i>; Parthian term, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυνάστης</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				171
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as a military term, at
			Athens, <i>the commander of the cavalry furnished by each tribe,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.69
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ φ.,</span> an oligarchical council at
			Epidamnus, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1301b22
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
